and Naehrig, Michael",
editor="Canteaut, Anne
and Standaert, Fran{\c{c}}ois-Xavier",
title="Sieving for Twin Smooth Integers with Solutions to the Prouhet-Tarry-Escott Problem",
booktitle="Advances in Cryptology -- EUROCRYPT 2021",
year="2021",
publisher="Springer International Publishing",
address="Cham",
pages="272--301",
abstract="We give a sieving algorithm for finding pairs of consecutive smooth numbers that utilizes solutions to the Prouhet-Tarry-Escott (PTE) problem. Any such solution induces two degree-n polynomials, a(x) and b(x), that differ by a constant integer C and completely split into linear factors in {\$}{\$}{\backslash}mathbb {\{}Z{\}}[x]{\$}{\$}Z[x]. It follows that for any {\$}{\$}{\backslash}ell {\backslash}in {\backslash}mathbb {\{}Z{\}}{\$}{\$}ℓ∈Zsuch that {\$}{\$}a({\backslash}ell ) {\backslash}equiv b({\backslash}ell ) {\backslash}equiv 0 {\backslash}bmod {\{}C{\}}{\$}{\$}a(ℓ)≡b(ℓ)≡0modC, the two integers {\$}{\$}a({\backslash}ell )/C{\$}{\$}a(ℓ)/Cand {\$}{\$}b({\backslash}ell )/C{\$}{\$}b(ℓ)/Cdiffer by 1 and necessarily contain n factors of roughly the same size. For a fixed smoothness bound B, restricting the search to pairs of integers that are parameterized in this way increases the probability that they are B-smooth. Our algorithm combines a simple sieve with parametrizations given by a collection of solutions to the PTE problem.",
isbn="978-3-030-77870-5"
}

